    <md:title>2.14.3: Self Check</md:title>
    <md:uuid>7776d065-f351-4b5e-9a6a-108bacd4ab91</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><newline/><para dir="ltr">A music store is shipping guitars and snare drums. </para><span id="docs-internal-guid-eba221b0-7fff-0811-4aab-876d1094b1c9">
  <list>
    <item>Each guitar weighs 6 pounds.</item>
    <item>Each snare drum weighs 14 pounds. </item>
    <item>The maximum weight of guitars and snare drums cannot be more than 120 pounds.</item>
    <item>The store needs to ship more than 10 total instruments.</item>
  </list>
  <para dir="ltr">Which of the following systems of inequalities describes the situation if \(x\) is the number of guitars and \(y\) is the number of snare drums?</para>
</span></section>
</content>
</document>
